{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775347121-sjX3czND4Gj7FN3s5NVQ","role":"assistant","created":1775347131,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a complex table. I can see there's data for Treasury bonds, corporate bonds, and municipal bonds across different years. Let me parse the data more carefully to find:\n\n1. August 1982 - need the \"new\" long-term Treasury bonds yield\n2. August 1981 - need the \"new\" long-term Treasury bonds yield\n\nLooking at the table:\n- The data seems to be organized in blocks by year: 1971, 1972, 1973, 1974, 1975, 1976, 1977, 1978, 1979, 1980, 1981, 1982\n- I can see there are footnotes about \"new\" bonds (4/ means one or more new long-term bonds added, 5/ means existing bond dropped)\n\nLooking at the 1981 column (for Aug. 1981):\n- For 1981, I see: \"Aug. | 13.61 | 16.34 | 12.11\"\n\nLooking at the 1982 column (for Aug. 1982):\n- The 1982 data seems incomplete in the first block (Aug shows \"nan\")\n- But then there's another section with weekly data for 1982\n\nLet me look at this more carefully. The first table seems to have data in blocks:\n- 1971, 1974, 1977, 1980 (first set of columns)\n- 1972, 1975, 1978, 1981 (second set of columns)\n- 1973, 1976, 1979, 1982 (third set of columns)\n\nSo for August 1981, it should be in the 1981 row under the \"1972, 1975, 1978, 1981\" block. Looking at that row, I see:\n\"Aug. | 5.59 | 7.59 | 5.19 | 4/7.11 | 9.71 | 6.88 | 4/5/7.88 | 8.83 | 5.81 | 13.61 | 16.34 | 12.11\"\n\n\nThe Treasury bond yield for August 1981 is 13.61%. The August 1982 data appears as \"nan\" in the main table, so I need to check the weekly data section to find that value.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_f703f22de6e74a2081a23719","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"grep -A5 \"1981\\|1982\" /app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1982_08_page_82.txt"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
