re carefully in the raw data to see if there's data for August 1982 somewhere.\n\nActually, I think I need to reconsider. The \"as of reported values on the end of the 1982 FY\" could mean we're looking at the data that was available at the end of fiscal year 1982, which would be September 1982 (since FY 1982 ended on September 30, 1982). But the question specifically asks for August 1982 and August 1981 yields.\n\nThe 1982 column in the monthly series table covers calendar year 1982, but it only shows data through July - August is missing. There are also weekly data points listed below the monthly table that might contain the August 1982 figure I'm looking for.\n\nLooking at the footnote explanations, numbers like \"4/\" and \"5/\" indicate new bonds added to the average or existing bonds removed from it. The Treasury bond yields themselves are based on closing bid quotations in the over-the-counter market, filtered for bonds that are neither due nor callable before 10 years and subject to normal tax and surtax.\n\nFor August 1981, the yield sits at 13.61%. However, August 1982 appears blank in the main table, so I need to examine the weekly data section to locate that figure. The subsequent section displays weekly data for February through July 1982, organized with Treasury bond yields, new Aa corporate bonds, and new Aa municipal bonds arranged chronologically. The footer shows August 2 has a value of 12.87, though the yield appears incomplete. Looking at the weekly data from July, I can see Treasury yields were recorded at 13.42 on the 2nd, 13.25 on the 9th, 12.98 on the 16th, 12.69 on the 23rd, and 12.87 on the 30th. Since the question asks about the monthly average for August 1982, I need to determine whether to use the August 1982 figure from the main table or calculate from these weekly observations. Let me search the full document for the August 1982 entry to clarify which value represents the monthly average.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"