asury Bulletin only provides monthly data through July 1982. I'll investigate whether September 1982 data offers a comparable reference point for the desired analysis.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_7a43a6e54c494090aad4305d","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport re\n\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1982_08_page_82.txt', 'r') as f:\n    content = f.read()\n\n# Search for August dates in weekly data\n# The weekly data has format like \"Feb. 5\", \"Feb. 12\", etc.\n# Find all week entries for any month\n\n# Let's find the second table with weekly data\ntable2_match = re.search(r'<table>.*?<tr><td>1982</td>.*?</table>', content, re.DOTALL)\nif table2_match:\n    table_content = table2_match.group(0)\n    # Find all dates and yields\n    print(\"Weekly data in second table:\")\n    print(table_content[:2000])\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
